A||||12||California Kid||Has anybody painted their interior switch buttons??||||1||
Z||000000||California Kid||12-10-2001||12:45 AM||||Curious if anyone (like me) got tired of looking at those ugly gray switch buttons and painted them. I'm playing with the idea of painting all of them.<P>Any feedback would be appreciated.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/californiakidsig_2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Cozmo||12-10-2001||01:23 AM||||Look around in your local boneyard for a '90s Bonneville.  They have switches (mirrors, windows, etc) that are the same form factor as a Fieros, and are MUCH higher quality...(some mods required to adapt them tho).<BR>PLUS they light up "Pontiac orange"!!!<BR>As far as the pod switches, you can find gloss black headlight switches, dimmer wheels and defog switches in many other GM cars.  The trunk release is another story....<BR>It has that cool lit Fiero silhouette on it and may be unique.  <P><P>------------------<BR><B>Bob Cardone</B><BR><B>Suncoast Fieros</B><BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/thankssig.jpg">   <BR><B>'85 2M6 SE Targa</B>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Nashco||12-10-2001||02:07 AM||||AusFiero painted his switches and it looked great.  I believe his were a metallic gray; he said they took a lot of thorough prep-work, but were fairly cut and dry.  Anybody happen to have a link?<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000003||Nashco||12-10-2001||02:11 AM||||Heh...used the search engine for ya <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Archives/Archive-000002/HTML/20010924-1-006816.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Archives/Archive-000002/HTML/20010924-1-006816.html</A> <P>At the bottom of the first page is the specifics.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
