Z||000007||AusFiero||12-10-2001||08:42 AM||||Well that saved me posting the link  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>It is fairly basic to do C Kid. Switches come apart easy.<P>------------------<BR>        <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero3.gif">       <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.fieroshop.com.au" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||1
Z||000008||Alex4mula||12-10-2001||08:50 AM||||I painted my power windows buttons(88 Formula) the same gray. Just sanded a little and cleaned well with acetone. The paint I used was prepared at a paint shop to match the interior gray. Results were excellent and no peeling or fading in any part in 9 months now.<P>------------------<BR>    Alex4mula<BR>:) Red-Original Owner & White-1/94 with PM (:||||reg||1
Z||000009||Doni Hagan||12-11-2001||05:58 PM||||COZMO is right about the Bonneville and other GM cars from the same period. Camaro/Firebird included. <P>Also, the power mirror switch in the 6000STE is the same as the fiero switch. Some mod is required, though. Forgive the fuzzy pic.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/CONSOLE.jpg"> <P>The only one I've had a problem finding is, as stated, the power trunk switch in black. I painted mine (mind you avoid the "lit" part) and it works fine! <p>[This message has been edited by Doni Hagan (edited 12-12-2001).]||||reg||1
